      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "Use the values in the table at \\( t = 10 \\) and \\( t = 15 \\) to approximate the rate of change of the balloon's height with respect to the amount of propane in its tank at time \\( t = 12.5 \\). Show the computations that lead to your answer, and indicate units of measure.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "-36 \\text{ feet per gallon}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "The rate of change of height with respect to propane is the change in B divided by the change in P over the same interval of time.",
               "latex": "\\frac{dB}{dP} \\approx \\frac{B(15) - B(10)}{P(15) - P(10)} = \\frac{420 - 330}{31.5 - 34.0} = \\frac{90}{-2.5} = -36"
